            <ArticleTitle>Alkene 1,2-Difunctionalization by Radical Alkenyl Migration.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>814-817</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/anie.201710397</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Transition-metal-free radical α-perfluoroalkylation with the accompanying vicinal β-alkenylation of unactivated alkenes is presented. These radical cascades proceed by means of 1,4- or 1,5-alkenyl migration by electron catalysis on readily accessed allylic alcohols. The reactions comprise a regioselective perfluoroalkyl radical addition with subsequent alkenyl migration and concomitant deprotonation to generate a ketyl radical anion that sustains the chain as a single-electron-transfer reducing reagent.</AbstractText>
